// The T1 world (docs/14 §tiers, docs/16 §plugin.toml capabilities).
//
// Everything a plugin tool can do is in this file. That is the point of the
// tier: "capability: only WIT imports we grant" — a capability that is not an
// import here does not exist for the guest, so it cannot be reached by a bug,
// a clever prompt, or a malicious plugin.
//
// v1 is deliberately tiny. Every import added here is a permanent promise to
// every installed plugin, and widening a world later is easy while narrowing it
// breaks people.
package panday:plugin@1.0.0;

interface host {
    /// Structured logging back into the harness. Content-free by convention
    /// (docs/21 T5): a plugin's log line lands in our spans, so it carries a
    /// level and a message and never gets to name a field of ours.
    log: func(level: string, message: string);
}

/// A plugin-provided tool.
///
/// JSON in, JSON out, because the tool's arguments already have a JSON Schema in
/// `plugin.toml` and the ToolRegistry speaks JSON (docs/13). A richer WIT record
/// would mean two schema languages for one contract.
world tool {
    import host;

    /// `args` is the JSON object the model produced. The `error` string is shown
    /// to the model as a tool error, so it is a message and not a code.
    export run: func(args: string) -> result<string, string>;
}
